# The domain the landing page is served on. Caddy reads this to decide which
# certificate to ask Let's Encrypt for, so it must be a name whose DNS A
# record already points at this host — otherwise the ACME challenge fails and
# the site never comes up. The bot is unaffected either way.
SCOUT_DOMAIN=scout.example.com

# Telegram bot token from @BotFather
TELEGRAM_BOT_TOKEN=

# Comma-separated Telegram user IDs allowed to use the bot (get yours from
# @userinfobot). This is the FOUNDER list: the people who set the bot up and
# pay for it. It is not the whole picture once invites are in use — everyone
# admitted through /invite lives in the database instead, and /invite status
# is the answer to "why can this person talk to the bot".
ALLOWED_TELEGRAM_USER_IDS=

# Optional: who sees everyone's numbers in /stat. Everyone else sees only
# their own. Defaults to the FIRST id in ALLOWED_TELEGRAM_USER_IDS, so set
# this explicitly if that list is not in the order you think it is. Every id
# here must also be in the allowlist.
#SCOUT_ADMIN_USER_IDS=

# MiniMax API key from https://www.minimax.io (used for the M3 model)
MINIMAX_API_KEY=

# Kagi API key from https://kagi.com/settings?p=api (paid, used for search/summarizer)
KAGI_API_KEY=

# Optional second search engine. Kagi and Perplexity find different small
# retailers, so with this set both are searched and the results merged.
PERPLEXITY_API_KEY=

# bol.com Marketing Catalog API (affiliate account -> Seller Dashboard >
# Account > Open API). Live catalogue search with current prices; both keys
# or neither. BOL_COUNTRY is NL or BE.
BOL_CLIENT_ID=
BOL_CLIENT_SECRET=
BOL_COUNTRY=NL

# Path to Chrome/Chromium for the headless fallback used when a shop blocks
# plain HTTP. Auto-detected when unset; the Docker image sets it. Without a
# browser the fallback is simply off.
SCOUT_CHROME=

# Optional: how many messages a day someone invited through /invite may send
# (default 20). Ids in ALLOWED_TELEGRAM_USER_IDS are exempt. This bounds each
# person; a round's capacity bounds how many people there are — opening a
# round is the moment to think about the bill. Counted over text and photo
# messages since midnight UTC.
#INVITE_DAILY_REQUESTS=20

# Optional: path to the DuckDB file for purchase memory (default: scout.duckdb)
#SCOUT_DB_PATH=scout.duckdb

# Optional: second-hand platforms for site-scoped search (default shown)
#SECONDHAND_SITES=ebay.com,marktplaats.nl,vinted.com

# Optional: eBay Browse API (developer.ebay.com -> Application Keys, Production keyset).
# Set BOTH: App ID (Client ID) and Cert ID (Client Secret). Enables live
# eBay prices/availability instead of unverified search snippets.
EBAY_CLIENT_ID=
EBAY_CLIENT_SECRET=
#EBAY_MARKETPLACE=EBAY_NL

# Optional: Duffel flight search (duffel.com -> Dashboard -> Access tokens).
# Enables live flight prices, times and baggage. Scout only ever searches —
# it never creates an order, so no passenger details or card details go
# anywhere near this key.
# A duffel_test_ key searches Duffel's fake airline for free and is the right
# way to try this out. A live key bills $0.005 per search once you exceed
# 1500 searches per booking made — with no bookings that is every search,
# which still comes to a few euro a month at household volumes.
DUFFEL_API_KEY=

# Optional booking fee, as a rate: 0.03 means 3%. Applied to the prices Scout
# quotes AND passed to Duffel's checkout, so the number shown is the number
# charged. Scout says in the reply that prices include it. Unset means no fee
# and no mention of one.
#DUFFEL_MARKUP_RATE=0.03

# Optional: Ignav fare search (ignav.com — free account, 1,000 requests, then
# $0.002 each, no rate limits). A second flights provider, merged into the
# same ranked list as Duffel and labelled row by row.
# Its prices are NOT bookable: Ignav's own docs say to show them as
# "from $299" and send the traveller to the seller's page for the live
# price. Scout marks them approximate/unconfirmed and warns whenever one
# undercuts a price somebody could actually pay.
# It also surfaces self-transfer itineraries (two separate tickets), which
# Duffel never returns.
IGNAV_API_KEY=
